.\" tar.1 -- GNU tar 1.14 as built for Amix (userland/packages/tar).
.\" Written for this package: GNU tar 1.14 documents itself in texinfo only.
.\" MIT licence, see LICENSE in userland/packages.
.TH TAR 1 "2026-10-30" "GNU tar 1.14" "Amix add-on commands"
.SH NAME
tar \- GNU tape archiver
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tar
.I operation
[\fIoption\fR]... [\fIfile\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tar
saves many files together in a single archive, and restores single files or
all of them from it.
This is GNU
.B tar
1.14, installed as
.BR /opt/amix/bin/tar .
It does not replace the stock SVR4
.B tar
in
.BR /usr/sbin ,
which stays as it is; this one is used when
.B /opt/amix/bin
comes before
.B /usr/sbin
in
.BR PATH .
.PP
Exactly one operation is given.
Options may be given as long options
.RB ( \-\-file=archive.tar ),
as short options
.RB ( "\-f archive.tar" ),
or in the old style, bundled into the first argument without a dash
.RB ( "tar cvf archive.tar dir" ).
An argument that is mandatory for a long option is mandatory for its short
option too.
.PP
The default archive is the standard input or output
.RB ( \-f\ \- ),
the default record size is 20 blocks of 512 bytes, and the default format for
new archives is
.BR gnu .
.SH OPERATIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-create
Create a new archive from the named files and directories.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-list
List the members of an archive.
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-extract ", " \-\-get
Extract members from an archive.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-diff ", " \-\-compare
Report differences between the archive and the file system.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-append
Append files to the end of an archive.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-update
Append only files newer than their copy in the archive.
.TP
.BR \-A ", " \-\-catenate ", " \-\-concatenate
Append other tar archives to an archive.
.TP
.B \-\-delete
Delete members from an archive (not on a tape).
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Archive and device
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-file= \fIarchive\fR
Use \fIarchive\fR: a file, a device, or
.B \-
for standard input or output.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-blocking\-factor= \fIn\fR
Write records of \fIn\fR x 512 bytes (default 20).
.TP
.BI \-\-record\-size= size
Write records of \fIsize\fR bytes, a multiple of 512.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-ignore\-zeros
Ignore zeroed blocks in the archive, which normally mean its end.
.TP
.BR \-B ", " \-\-read\-full\-records
Reblock as the archive is read (for pipes).
.TP
.BR \-M ", " \-\-multi\-volume
Create, list or extract a multi-volume archive.
.TP
.BR \-L ", " \-\-tape\-length= \fIn\fR
Change volumes after \fIn\fR x 1024 bytes.
.TP
.BR \-F ", " \-\-info\-script= \fIfile\fR ", " \-\-new\-volume\-script= \fIfile\fR
Run \fIfile\fR at the end of each volume (implies
.BR \-M ).
.TP
.BI \-\-volno\-file= file
Keep the volume number in \fIfile\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-force\-local
Treat an archive name with a colon as a local file.
.TP
.BI \-\-rsh\-command= command ", \-\-rmt\-command=" command
The remote shell and the remote tape server for a
.IB host : file
archive; see BUGS.
.SS Compression
.TP
.BR \-z ", " \-\-gzip ", " \-\-ungzip
Filter the archive through
.BR gzip ,
found on
.BR PATH .
Install the
.B gzip
package for it.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-bzip2
Filter the archive through
.BR bzip2 ,
found on
.B PATH
(the
.B bzip2
package).
.TP
.BR \-Z ", " \-\-compress ", " \-\-uncompress
Filter the archive through the stock
.BR compress .
.TP
.BI \-\-use\-compress\-program= program
Filter the archive through \fIprogram\fR, which must accept
.BR \-d .
.SS Format
.TP
.BI \-\-format= format
Create the archive in \fIformat\fR:
.B v7
(the old V7 format),
.B oldgnu
(GNU tar 1.12 and older),
.B gnu
(GNU tar 1.13, the default),
.B ustar
(POSIX 1003.1-1988) or
.B posix
(POSIX 1003.1-2001, pax).
.TP
.BR \-\-old\-archive ", " \-\-portability
The same as
.BR \-\-format=v7 .
.TP
.B \-\-posix
The same as
.BR \-\-format=posix .
.TP
.BI \-\-pax\-option " keyword" [[:]= value ][, ...]
Control the pax keywords of a
.B posix
archive.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-label= \fIname\fR
Give a new archive the volume name \fIname\fR; when reading, a pattern the
volume name must match.
.SS File selection
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-directory= \fIdir\fR
Change to \fIdir\fR before the following names.
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-files\-from= \fIfile\fR
Read the names to archive or extract from \fIfile\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-null
The names read by
.B \-T
are terminated by NUL characters.
.TP
.BI \-\-exclude= pattern
Leave out files matching \fIpattern\fR.
.TP
.BR \-X ", " \-\-exclude\-from= \fIfile\fR
Leave out files matching the patterns listed in \fIfile\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-anchored ", " \-\-no\-anchored ", " \-\-ignore\-case ", " \-\-no\-ignore\-case ", " \-\-wildcards ", " \-\-no\-wildcards ", " \-\-wildcards\-match\-slash ", " \-\-no\-wildcards\-match\-slash
How exclusion patterns match: from the start of the name (the default) or
after any
.BR / ;
case sensitive (the default) or not; with wildcards (the default) or as
plain strings; wildcards matching
.B /
(the default) or not.
.TP
.BR \-P ", " \-\-absolute\-names
Keep the leading
.B /
of file names.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-dereference
Archive the files symbolic links point to, not the links.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-recursion
Do not descend into directories.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-one\-file\-system
Stay in the file system of each named directory when creating.
.TP
.BR \-K ", " \-\-starting\-file= \fIname\fR
Begin at member \fIname\fR of the archive.
.TP
.BI \-\-strip\-path= n
Strip \fIn\fR leading components from member names when extracting.
.TP
.BR \-N ", " \-\-newer= \fIdate\fR ", " \-\-after\-date= \fIdate\fR
Archive only files newer than \fIdate\fR, a date or the name of a file
starting with
.B /
or
.B .
whose date is taken.
.TP
.BI \-\-newer\-mtime= date
The same, comparing the modification time only.
.TP
.BR \-G ", " \-\-incremental
Handle an old GNU-format incremental backup.
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-listed\-incremental= \fIfile\fR
Handle a new GNU-format incremental backup, keeping its state in \fIfile\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-occurrence [= \fIn\fR ]
With
.BR \-\-delete ,
.BR \-\-diff ,
.B \-\-extract
or
.B \-\-list
and named members, act on the \fIn\fRth occurrence of each (default 1).
.SS Extraction
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-keep\-old\-files
Do not replace existing files.
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-newer\-files
Do not replace existing files that are newer than their archive copies.
.TP
.B \-\-overwrite
Overwrite existing files.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-overwrite\-dir
Keep the metadata of existing directories.
.TP
.BR \-U ", " \-\-unlink\-first
Remove each file before extracting over it.
.TP
.B \-\-recursive\-unlink
Empty a directory hierarchy before extracting a directory over it.
.TP
.BR \-O ", " \-\-to\-stdout
Extract to the standard output.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-modification\-time
Do not restore the modification time.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-same\-permissions ", " \-\-preserve\-permissions
Restore the permissions recorded in the archive.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-same\-permissions
Do not restore the recorded permissions.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-same\-order ", " \-\-preserve\-order
The names to extract are in the archive's order.
.TP
.B \-\-preserve
The same as
.B \-p
and
.BR \-s .
.TP
.BR \-\-same\-owner ", " \-\-no\-same\-owner
Restore the recorded owners (the default for root), or extract as yourself.
.TP
.BR \-\-backup [= \fIcontrol\fR "], \-\-suffix=" \fIsuffix\fR
Back up a file before replacing it; see ENVIRONMENT.
.SS Creation
.TP
.BI \-\-owner= name ", \-\-group=" name
Record \fIname\fR as the owner or group of added files.
.TP
.BI \-\-mode= changes
Record the symbolic mode \fIchanges\fR applied to added files.
.TP
.B \-\-numeric\-owner
Record and use numeric user and group ids only.
.TP
.B \-\-atime\-preserve
Keep the access times of archived files.
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-sparse
Handle sparse files efficiently.
.TP
.B \-\-remove\-files
Remove files after adding them.
.TP
.BR \-W ", " \-\-verify
Verify the archive after writing it.
.TP
.B \-\-ignore\-failed\-read
Do not exit non-zero for unreadable files.
.SS Output
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
List the files processed; twice for a long listing.
.TP
.B \-\-totals
Print the bytes written when creating.
.TP
.BR \-\-checkpoint ", " \-\-check\-links ", " \-\-utc
Print directory names while reading; report hard links not all archived;
print dates in UTC.
.TP
.BI \-\-index\-file= file
Write the verbose output to \fIfile\fR.
.TP
.BR \-R ", " \-\-block\-number
Show the block number in each message.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-interactive ", " \-\-confirmation
Ask before every action.
.TP
.B \-o
When creating, the same as
.BR \-\-old\-archive ;
when extracting, the same as
.BR \-\-no\-same\-owner .
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-\-version
Print the full option list, or the version, and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TAR_OPTIONS
Options read before those on the command line.
.TP
.BR SIMPLE_BACKUP_SUFFIX ", " VERSION_CONTROL
The backup suffix (default
.BR ~ )
and the kind of backup:
.BR t " or " numbered ,
.BR nil " or " existing ,
.BR never " or " simple .
.TP
.B PATH
Where
.BR gzip ,
.B bzip2
and
.B compress
are found for
.BR \-z ,
.B \-j
and
.BR \-Z .
.SH AMIX NOTES
.B tar
reads and writes the base-256 sizes and ids, and the long names, of modern
GNU and POSIX archives.
.PP
Owner and group names are looked up by
.BR tar 's
own readers of
.B /etc/passwd
and
.BR /etc/group ,
not by the stock C library.
.PP
An archive id above the range of the SVR4 user id type is read and listed
exactly, but the kernel refuses to set it: such a file is extracted owned by
root, and
.B tar
exits with status 2.
.PP
Shrinking an archive in place
.RB ( \-\-delete )
truncates it on a block boundary and writes the tail back, so the stock
kernel's truncation fault is not reached.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B tar \-cf archive.tar foo bar
Create
.B archive.tar
from
.B foo
and
.BR bar .
.TP
.B tar \-tvf archive.tar
List
.B archive.tar
verbosely.
.TP
.B tar \-xzf src.tar.gz \-C /tmp
Extract a gzip-compressed archive into
.BR /tmp .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 when some files differ
.RB ( \-\-diff ),
2 on a fatal error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /opt/amix/bin/tar
This program.
.TP
.B /opt/amix/doc/tar
Its licence, NEWS and README.
.SH BUGS
Remote archives
.RI ( host : file )
have no default remote shell in this build: one must be given with
.BR \-\-rsh\-command ,
and the remote host must provide
.B rmt
.RB ( \-\-rmt\-command );
no
.B rmt
is installed here.
Remote archives are untested on Amix.
.PP
Tape ioctls are not built (the system has no
.BR <sys/mtio.h> ).
.PP
.B \-\-totals
shows the rate as
.B ?/s
for a run under one second.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gzip (1),
.BR bzip2 (1),
.BR compress (1).
The full manual is GNU tar's texinfo manual; this build ships its NEWS and
README in
.BR /opt/amix/doc/tar .
